            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the issue!\n\nThe `doc/tags` entry in the `.gitignore` file is (reasonably) only there to make it easier for contributors to *not* commit tags into the repository. Otherwise I don't really see a problem in having uncommitted `doc/tags` file in the plugin people use on disk.\n\nIf that is for some reason the problem, adding `doc/tags` in the global `.gitignore` is a reasonable solution here (and what I use).\n\n> Creating a PR in the mini.icons repository is restricted to collaborators, so I can't send a PR.\n\nAnd that is precisely why there was no need for a `.gitignore` file there. But to be fair, that was mostly an oversight which might be fixed in the future. As this is not really an issue with 'mini.nvim' itself, I'll close this for now with a plan to return to this in the near future.",
